# SHARD Orphan-Page Carving Test Data Manifest — ambiguous-schema / tight-mode variant
# Database: carving_ambiguous_tables.db
# Created by: create_carving_ambiguous_tables.py
# Created: 2026-08-17
#
# table_a and table_b share byte-identical column shape. A bulk DELETE of
# ids 150-450 from table_a only frees one of its leaf pages outright (page
# 7), leaving its original 54 cells (ids 447-500) intact but unreachable.
# table_b is never touched. Loose (affinity-only) matching cannot tell the
# two tables' records apart; tight (observed-data-narrowed) matching can,
# since table_a's `num` column is always a 1-byte integer and table_b's is
# always a 4-byte integer. PRAGMA secure_delete=OFF was set explicitly; the
# file was closed normally (no WAL involved).

